 sits on the vertical line x=11. It emits row 12, with rings at x=2, 7 and 16.\n\n**Teaching stages.** The program emits one canvas after each line is drawn, one after each ring is stamped, and then the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    out = g.copy()\n    frames = components(g == 3)\n    centres = []\n    for cells in frames:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(cells)\n        centres.append(((y0 + y1) // 2, (x0 + x1) // 2))\n    for cy, cx in centres:\n        vertical = False\n        for yy in (cy - 2, cy + 2):\n            if 0 <= yy < H and g[yy, cx] == 2:\n                vertical = True\n        if vertical:\n            path = [(cy, x) for x in range(W)]\n        else:\n            path = [(y, cx) for y in range(H)]\n        for (y, x) in path:\n            if g[y, x] == 0:\n                out[y, x] = 1\n        emit(out, f\"Frame at ({cy},{cx}) sits on a {'vertical' if vertical else 'horizontal'} 2-line; \"\n                  f\"draw a perpendicular line of 1 through its centre over background.\")\n        for (y, x) in path:\n            if g[y, x] == 2 and (y, x) != (cy, cx):\n                for dy in (-1, 0, 1):\n                    for dx in (-1, 0, 1):\n                        if dy == 0 and dx == 0:\n                            continue\n                        yy, xx = y + dy, x + dx\n                        if 0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W and g[yy, xx] != 3:\n                            out[yy, xx] = 1\n                emit(out, f\"The new line crosses a 2-line at ({y},{x}); stamp a 3x3 ring of 1 around it.\")\n    emit(out, \"All frames have emitted their lines and crossing rings.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Teaching stages.** The program emits one canvas after each line is drawn, one after each ring is stamped, and then the final grid."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"The new line crosses a 2-line at (2,9); stamp a 3x3 ring of 1 around it."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"The new line crosses a 2-line at (11,3); stamp a 3x3 ring of 1 around it."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"It emits row 2, with rings at x=7, 11 and 16."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It emits row 12, with rings at x=2, 7 and 16."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"All frames have emitted their lines and crossing rings."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"03277ddaf90906bf702198c3d77ed525a994cd5950e9a68286dcc57b6e9e2804","task_sha256":"6f24c1dac94d0024bbdd87a383139110935fce9dcdfc99256e2d7707bc218d21","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
